menu "Shelly wall switch input"

    config SHELLY_SWITCH_ACTIVE_HIGH
        bool "SW reads HIGH when the switch is on (pressed)"
        default y
        help
            Which level of the SW input means the wall switch is on, or a push
            button is pressed. Only the Follow and Push button switch modes use
            it (docs/BUTTON-AND-LED.md, Wall switch modes); Toggle acts on any
            change. The default comes from the hardware-tested ESPHome
            configuration for these boards (SW not inverted); it is not verified
            with this firmware. If Follow runs backwards, turn this off.

endmenu
